WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.467
Switch reminders and notices on or off, and set their timing.

00:00:05.167 --> 00:00:08.733
What runs. Every automation, one card each.

00:00:09.233 --> 00:00:21.433
Estimate follow-ups. No answer to an estimate: Email 1 after the days you set, Email 2 later, then a call ticket for the office. Estimates older than the last number are skipped.

00:00:21.933 --> 00:00:25.500
The switch. Turns it on or off and saves at once.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:33.533
Its timing. Change a number and the flow above follows it. Press the Save button that appears on the card to keep it.

00:00:34.033 --> 00:00:48.333
Past-due reminders. One statement per customer listing what's open: first after the days past due, then every few days, up to the number set; then a collection call. It can include SA balances.

00:00:48.833 --> 00:01:01.600
Appointment reminders. The day before, at the hour you set (0–23, 10 = 10 am), by email and by text when texts are on. Moving the appointment sends the new time.

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:12.300
Job start notice. The day before a crew's first day on a job. "Crews usually arrive" is the wording for when they come. Maintenance visits don't get one.

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:20.267
"We've arrived". Sent when the crew lead starts the job on the phone, with the arrival photo. Once a day per job.

00:01:20.767 --> 00:01:32.067
Accepted online → deposit. When a customer signs the online estimate, the job, contract and payment schedule are made and the deposit invoice is emailed.

00:01:32.567 --> 00:01:40.367
Card declined. Marking a card as declined emails the customer to update it and gives the office a call ticket.

00:01:40.867 --> 00:01:52.033
Satisfaction survey. A short survey link the days you set after a job is complete. A score at or below your number opens a ticket so someone calls the customer.

00:01:52.533 --> 00:02:04.567
Website requests. Off: requests wait on My day for someone to accept. On: genuine-looking ones become a customer and a ticket at once, for the person in "Tickets go to".

00:02:05.067 --> 00:02:12.367
Sent and wording. Each card says how many went out in the last 30 days. Edit wording opens its message.

00:02:12.867 --> 00:02:18.467
That's it. You can play this tour in the app any time: press Help, and ask in your own words.
